1
00:00:01,874 --> 00:00:05,533
(Episode 12)

2
00:00:22,446 --> 00:00:24,910
You've been here before, haven't you?

3
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:27,664
We weren't able to reach you
since we didn't have your contact.

4
00:00:27,664 --> 00:00:28,745
Why?

5
00:00:28,745 --> 00:00:31,780
Please see your doctor. He's still here.

6
00:00:33,111 --> 00:00:34,643
What is going on?

7
00:00:42,176 --> 00:00:43,443
What?

8
00:00:43,443 --> 00:00:45,324
I think you have leukemia.

9
00:00:47,218 --> 00:00:49,091
Leukemia is...

10
00:00:49,091 --> 00:00:50,403
You know what it is.

11
00:00:50,403 --> 00:00:53,282
Do you have any family members
who had this?

12
00:00:53,282 --> 00:00:55,380
This disease most likely
runs in the family.

13
00:00:56,268 --> 00:00:57,339
I see.

14
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:04,898
I heard my father passed away from it.

15
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:12,362
It is cancer, isn't it?

16
00:01:16,848 --> 00:01:20,659
Are you sure I have that?

17
00:01:23,305 --> 00:01:26,549
I'll be sure once you get reexaminations.

18
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,972
Miss, get off.

19
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:32,793
I think I need to go to Seoul.

20
00:03:34,039 --> 00:03:37,735
My mom left being so mad.

21
00:03:37,735 --> 00:03:39,225
I need to comfort her.

22
00:03:42,269 --> 00:03:43,269
Okay.

23
00:03:45,095 --> 00:03:46,313
I will take you.

24
00:03:49,245 --> 00:03:51,049
Don't you have anything to say to me?

25
00:03:57,942 --> 00:03:59,233
I see.

26
00:04:02,542 --> 00:04:05,921
How long do I have to see Eun Seo?

27
00:04:06,814 --> 00:04:10,280
For how long are you going to meet her?

28
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:12,907
Tell me. For how long?

29
00:04:14,648 --> 00:04:20,267
How long do I have to see her
reflected in your eyes?

30
00:04:22,264 --> 00:04:23,745
Tell me.

31
00:04:23,745 --> 00:04:25,769
Say something.

32
00:04:28,303 --> 00:04:29,715
Isn't it enough for you?

33
00:04:34,073 --> 00:04:36,354
Isn't it enough for you that I'm with you?

34
00:04:39,976 --> 00:04:43,169
Then, let's go to the U.S.
when this semester is over.

35
00:04:44,048 --> 00:04:47,183
What do you think?
Is this still not enough?

36
00:04:47,183 --> 00:04:49,372
Once we go there,
we won't ever come back here.

37
00:04:50,354 --> 00:04:54,007
What about this?
Is this still not enough for you?

38
00:04:57,380 --> 00:05:02,824
You mean your heart will be with her.

39
00:05:06,869 --> 00:05:09,640
You just can't tell me
that you'll love me with your heart.

40
00:05:16,876 --> 00:05:20,134
You are the one I chose.

41
00:05:20,134 --> 00:05:21,912
That's all I can say, Yu Mi.

42
00:05:24,797 --> 00:05:25,937
I'm sorry.

43
00:05:29,421 --> 00:05:30,711
It doesn't matter.

44
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:34,734
It does not matter.
I won't ever let you go.

45
00:05:35,798 --> 00:05:39,799
I will not let you go,
no matter what happens.

46
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:42,711
I will be back soon.

47
00:06:09,822 --> 00:06:10,832
Yu Mi.

48
00:06:13,212 --> 00:06:14,288
Yu Mi.

49
00:06:20,061 --> 00:06:21,241
Yu Mi.

50
00:06:22,061 --> 00:06:24,054
It's just two months.

51
00:06:24,054 --> 00:06:27,650
We're going to the U.S. in two months.

52
00:06:32,055 --> 00:06:33,224
I will give you a ride.

53
00:07:20,443 --> 00:07:22,596
Be careful.

54
00:07:22,596 --> 00:07:25,148
And don't work too hard
on your business trip.

55
00:07:25,148 --> 00:07:27,571
Don't worry. It's only for a week.

56
00:07:27,571 --> 00:07:29,485
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

57
00:07:29,485 --> 00:07:31,676
I'll drive you to the airport.

58
00:07:31,676 --> 00:07:33,886
- Thanks, Dad.
- Okay, let's go.

59
00:08:07,561 --> 00:08:09,456
Eun Seo, what brings you here?

60
00:08:09,456 --> 00:08:11,134
Didn't you go to work today?

61
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:13,445
No.

62
00:08:13,445 --> 00:08:15,302
Why not? What's wrong?

63
00:08:15,302 --> 00:08:16,425
Are you feeling unwell?

64
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:21,664
You guessed that so easily.

65
00:08:23,350 --> 00:08:25,467
I got a cold.

66
00:08:25,467 --> 00:08:28,578
Did you? Let me see.

67
00:08:28,578 --> 00:08:31,732
I think you have a fever.

68
00:08:31,732 --> 00:08:35,957
Eun Seo, why don't you lay down on my bed?

69
00:09:08,168 --> 00:09:09,717
What is this?

70
00:09:10,370 --> 00:09:13,626
Why is there so much food?

71
00:09:13,626 --> 00:09:16,347
It's been a while since I came home early.

72
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:17,788
Do you have money to waste?

73
00:09:18,666 --> 00:09:20,836
I'm sorry. It's just for today.

74
00:09:22,057 --> 00:09:23,103
And...

75
00:09:26,707 --> 00:09:28,692
What is it?

76
00:09:29,843 --> 00:09:33,243
Mom, let's have a drink together.

77
00:09:34,034 --> 00:09:35,109
What?

78
00:09:48,378 --> 00:09:49,565
I love it.

79
00:09:54,377 --> 00:09:57,030
You can't even drink.

80
00:09:58,868 --> 00:10:01,251
I can drink.

81
00:10:01,251 --> 00:10:03,761
- For you, Mom.
- Okay, fill it up.

82
00:10:15,615 --> 00:10:17,415
It's good.

83
00:10:17,415 --> 00:10:18,602
Dad.

84
00:10:25,406 --> 00:10:26,467
Your father?

85
00:10:30,806 --> 00:10:35,288
How long did it take before he passed away
after the diagnosis?

86
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:39,521
Why are you asking that?

87
00:10:40,686 --> 00:10:45,633
I'm just curious.

88
00:10:47,982 --> 00:10:50,842
Because he died before I was born.

89
00:10:56,575 --> 00:10:57,883
Was it soon?

90
00:11:00,303 --> 00:11:01,484
I'm not sure.

91
00:11:04,403 --> 00:11:05,812
I can't remember it for sure.

92
00:11:08,441 --> 00:11:11,821
Was it longer than two months?

93
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:15,605
It took a while.

94
00:11:17,161 --> 00:11:19,549
Also, it took a lot of money.

95
00:11:23,857 --> 00:11:25,790
Was he that bad?

96
00:11:27,300 --> 00:11:29,051
He really was.

97
00:11:29,051 --> 00:11:31,409
He used to break things
almost all the time.

98
00:11:31,409 --> 00:11:33,619
He was a drunkard and a gambler.

99
00:11:33,619 --> 00:11:35,388
He was the worst.

100
00:11:36,661 --> 00:11:38,824
The reason for his dying
from that disease was,

101
00:11:38,824 --> 00:11:41,325
I think, a form of punishment.

102
00:11:48,019 --> 00:11:49,356
I see.

103
00:11:52,057 --> 00:11:53,580
He got punished.

104
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:59,740
Dad also got punished.

105
00:12:04,129 --> 00:12:06,966
What are you talking about?

106
00:12:08,571 --> 00:12:11,149
No, it's nothing.

107
00:12:19,644 --> 00:12:20,745
Mom.

108
00:12:23,543 --> 00:12:27,057
I have made you upset, haven't I?

109
00:12:30,639 --> 00:12:32,285
After you sent Sin Ae away,

110
00:12:34,066 --> 00:12:37,020
you were upset while you raised me, right?

111
00:12:42,873 --> 00:12:48,500
There are far more things I did wrong...

112
00:12:49,689 --> 00:12:51,867
than I did well, while raising you.

113
00:12:53,737 --> 00:12:57,988
What are you saying?
You haven't done anything wrong.

114
00:13:04,153 --> 00:13:09,612
I wish I had been with you
since I was born.

115
00:13:11,401 --> 00:13:13,762
No way.

116
00:13:13,762 --> 00:13:16,845
Your other mom would wail
upon hearing that.

117
00:13:17,714 --> 00:13:20,019
No.

118
00:13:21,417 --> 00:13:24,635
It would have been better...

119
00:13:24,635 --> 00:13:28,102
if I had lived with one family
since I was born.

120
00:13:30,612 --> 00:13:32,195
It would have been good for you...

121
00:13:33,426 --> 00:13:37,652
and also good for the other mom.

122
00:13:42,992 --> 00:13:46,213
There wouldn't have been
this much regret on my part.

123
00:13:53,848 --> 00:13:55,146
Are you...

124
00:13:57,705 --> 00:14:00,476
still thinking of your brother?

125
00:14:03,226 --> 00:14:04,226
No.

126
00:14:13,554 --> 00:14:14,885
It's so bitter.

127
00:14:18,188 --> 00:14:22,223
Mom, do you want to sing together?

128
00:14:25,802 --> 00:14:29,843
My pale pink skirt is

129
00:14:29,843 --> 00:14:32,510
Fluttering

130
00:14:34,572 --> 00:14:38,983
In the spring wind

131
00:14:42,092 --> 00:14:46,708
Biting my dress string

132
00:14:46,708 --> 00:14:49,766
Again today

133
00:14:52,131 --> 00:14:55,651
On the village shrine road

134
00:14:55,651 --> 00:14:59,995
Visited by spring maidens

135
00:14:59,995 --> 00:15:04,009
When the flowers bloom

136
00:15:05,013 --> 00:15:08,113
We laugh together

137
00:15:10,211 --> 00:15:14,094
When the flowers fall

138
00:15:14,094 --> 00:15:16,694
We cry together

139
00:15:19,452 --> 00:15:26,449
With that sweet vow

140
00:15:29,542 --> 00:15:36,059
Spring days are gone

141
00:15:46,502 --> 00:15:47,608
Jun Seo.

142
00:15:53,271 --> 00:15:54,827
How could I...

143
00:15:58,553 --> 00:16:02,317
not think of you, even for a second?

144
00:16:06,177 --> 00:16:07,225
I can't, right?

145
00:16:10,634 --> 00:16:14,061
Yes, I have about two months left.

146
00:16:15,657 --> 00:16:19,968
Yes, once I go to the U.S. this time,

147
00:16:22,934 --> 00:16:25,161
I don't have plans to ever come back.

148
00:16:29,486 --> 00:16:32,033
I will visit you before I leave.

149
00:16:32,846 --> 00:16:33,846
Yes.

150
00:16:35,462 --> 00:16:36,522
Yes.

151
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:58,682
It's just two months.

152
00:17:58,682 --> 00:18:00,979
We're going to the U.S. in two months.

153
00:19:05,145 --> 00:19:07,128
Stop smiling. You'll grow on me.

154
00:19:07,128 --> 00:19:08,835
Don't smile when you're leaving
for the U.S. soon.

155
00:19:11,737 --> 00:19:12,947
Did Yu Mi come?

156
00:19:14,481 --> 00:19:16,035
I don't think she's coming.

157
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:22,788
She's planning to get her injured hand
examined while in Seoul.

158
00:19:22,788 --> 00:19:24,874
I think she'll come today or tomorrow.

159
00:19:24,874 --> 00:19:25,874
Is that so?

160
00:19:26,441 --> 00:19:29,621
Isn't it a good thing that
she keeps checking her hand?

161
00:19:33,812 --> 00:19:35,222
I hope things turn out well.

162
00:19:37,882 --> 00:19:39,239
They will.

163
00:19:39,723 --> 00:19:41,006
(Check Account Balance)

164
00:19:41,006 --> 00:19:42,006
(Please enter your four-digit PIN.)

165
00:19:51,265 --> 00:19:55,189
My eyes hurt since I watched movies
all night again.

166
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:58,119
Did you rent movies again?

167
00:19:58,119 --> 00:20:00,034
Because of the guy at the rental store.

168
00:20:01,870 --> 00:20:05,113
Why do you like him?

169
00:20:06,903 --> 00:20:11,414
Dimples, a blue shirt, and ripped jeans.

170
00:20:11,414 --> 00:20:14,257
He is gorgeous.
I think he is my first love.

171
00:20:14,670 --> 00:20:18,133
I don't think that is love.

172
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:19,133
Why not?

173
00:20:19,461 --> 00:20:20,702
It's not love.

174
00:20:22,397 --> 00:20:26,704
They say that if it's true love,
you don't need any reasons.

175
00:20:26,704 --> 00:20:27,771
Is that so?

176
00:20:28,617 --> 00:20:30,500
It's not like that in the movies.

177
00:20:32,441 --> 00:20:34,771
- Kang Hee.
- Yes.

178
00:20:36,933 --> 00:20:38,977
Among sad movies,

179
00:20:41,094 --> 00:20:43,604
is there a movie in which
the main character dies?

180
00:20:44,983 --> 00:20:46,140
There are a lot of them.

181
00:20:47,569 --> 00:20:50,337
"Love Story," "Take All of Me,"

182
00:20:50,337 --> 00:20:53,824
"The Letter," and "Christmas in August."

183
00:20:53,824 --> 00:20:55,401
What other ones are there?

184
00:20:57,935 --> 00:21:01,180
Do they all die from cancer?

185
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:04,693
Most of them do. Why?

186
00:21:05,329 --> 00:21:06,517
Then,

187
00:21:08,696 --> 00:21:11,906
in the movie,

188
00:21:11,906 --> 00:21:15,926
does it say how much it costs
to treat cancer, by any chance?

189
00:21:20,121 --> 00:21:25,221
Do I need surgery to live?

190
00:21:25,729 --> 00:21:28,708
That is the only option at this point.

191
00:21:31,178 --> 00:21:32,178
Right.

192
00:21:33,591 --> 00:21:35,986
I see.

193
00:21:36,327 --> 00:21:38,827
First of all, you need to rest.

194
00:21:38,827 --> 00:21:41,828
Be careful not to get bruises.

195
00:21:41,828 --> 00:21:45,084
Also, be careful not to bleed,
and watch out for tartar on your teeth.

196
00:21:45,084 --> 00:21:47,317
You may have intermittent bouts of pain.

197
00:21:47,317 --> 00:21:49,534
When you experience pain,
come straight to the hospital.

198
00:21:51,765 --> 00:21:52,888
And...

199
00:21:56,853 --> 00:22:01,774
How much will it cost for the treatments?

200
00:22:02,908 --> 00:22:06,423
I am not sure.
It could be tens of thousands of dollars.

201
00:22:07,619 --> 00:22:08,619
What did you say?

202
00:22:10,093 --> 00:22:11,375
Tens of thousands of dollars?

203
00:22:40,492 --> 00:22:41,750
Choi Eun Seo.

204
00:22:44,854 --> 00:22:46,877
What's going on?

205
00:22:46,877 --> 00:22:48,061
What?

206
00:22:48,061 --> 00:22:50,672
You're fired as of today.

207
00:22:51,556 --> 00:22:54,014
What? I am fired?

208
00:22:54,405 --> 00:22:58,294
I think it's
Director Han Tae Seok's order.

209
00:22:58,294 --> 00:22:59,639
Don't you know that?

210
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:22,075
Who is this?

211
00:23:23,545 --> 00:23:24,605
Are you Choi Eun Seo?

212
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:26,757
Tae Seok.

213
00:23:27,434 --> 00:23:30,184
I told you not to call me like that.

214
00:23:30,184 --> 00:23:32,035
Are you that stupid?

215
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:33,473
Am I fired?

216
00:23:33,473 --> 00:23:35,822
How could you do it without any grounds?

217
00:23:37,001 --> 00:23:40,317
Do you think only you can do
whatever you want, but I can't?

218
00:23:41,843 --> 00:23:43,001
This is me.

219
00:23:43,001 --> 00:23:46,571
Aren't you happy not to see me anymore?

220
00:23:46,571 --> 00:23:47,604
Aren't you?

221
00:23:47,604 --> 00:23:48,807
Tae Seok.

222
00:23:48,807 --> 00:23:49,832
Look at me.

223
00:23:51,278 --> 00:23:52,497
Look at me.

224
00:23:53,359 --> 00:23:57,210
I'm not your plaything.

225
00:23:58,406 --> 00:23:59,895
I've been thinking.

226
00:23:59,895 --> 00:24:02,371
About what could be
the most valuable thing to you.

227
00:24:03,086 --> 00:24:04,866
And funnily enough, it's money.

228
00:24:06,198 --> 00:24:09,214
If so, that is my strongest asset.

229
00:24:09,214 --> 00:24:11,450
Why did I take such a long way
to get here?

230
00:24:12,710 --> 00:24:16,216
Love? Don't be ridiculous.

231
00:24:17,207 --> 00:24:20,152
I will buy that. I will pay for it.

232
00:24:23,005 --> 00:24:24,632
How much is your love?

233
00:24:27,141 --> 00:24:28,568
How much do you think?

234
00:24:31,949 --> 00:24:35,080
How much can you afford?

235
00:24:41,094 --> 00:24:42,192
I...

236
00:24:45,352 --> 00:24:46,857
need money.

237
00:24:49,383 --> 00:24:54,737
I really need money.

238
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:01,282
How much can you offer me?

239
00:25:15,671 --> 00:25:17,536
How much can you pay me?

240
00:25:21,223 --> 00:25:23,024
How much can you pay?

241
00:25:25,759 --> 00:25:31,345
How much should I charge you for me?

242
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:10,487
Mom.

243
00:26:10,487 --> 00:26:13,803
Why did you come home this early?

244
00:26:14,935 --> 00:26:16,853
Aren't you feeling well?

245
00:26:16,853 --> 00:26:18,299
Did you leave work early?

246
00:26:21,087 --> 00:26:25,353
I quit.

247
00:26:25,775 --> 00:26:28,170
What? Do you quit?

248
00:26:28,170 --> 00:26:30,673
Get over here. Come here.

249
00:26:30,673 --> 00:26:34,442
When you dump the rich man,
you should work to make money.

250
00:26:34,442 --> 00:26:36,010
No, Jong Chul.

251
00:26:36,010 --> 00:26:40,116
How ungrateful you are.

252
00:26:40,116 --> 00:26:42,277
Stop, Jong Chul. Stop hitting me.

253
00:26:42,277 --> 00:26:43,917
You can't hit me, Jong Chul.

254
00:26:43,917 --> 00:26:45,493
I shouldn't get bruises anymore,
Jong Chul.

255
00:26:45,493 --> 00:26:47,292
Jong Chul, stop it.

256
00:26:47,292 --> 00:26:48,417
Get out of my way.

257
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:52,479
Don't you want to get beaten?

258
00:26:52,479 --> 00:26:54,557
Then, go out and make money.

259
00:26:54,557 --> 00:26:56,672
No, please.
I really shouldn't get bruises, Jong Chul.

260
00:26:56,672 --> 00:26:57,840
Jong Chul, please.

261
00:26:57,840 --> 00:27:00,738
Eun Seo, run away while I hold him.

262
00:27:00,738 --> 00:27:01,986
Why won't you come here?

263
00:27:01,986 --> 00:27:04,319
- Jong Chul.
- Get out of my way. Let me go!

264
00:27:04,977 --> 00:27:05,977
Get out of my way!

265
00:27:10,303 --> 00:27:13,296
Are you going to where your fiancé is?

266
00:27:13,296 --> 00:27:16,329
Yes, I'm going to the airport now.

267
00:27:16,329 --> 00:27:19,412
I'm glad you have good news to tell him.

268
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:21,547
What?

269
00:27:24,257 --> 00:27:25,322
That means...

270
00:27:25,322 --> 00:27:27,899
Your test results came out really well.

271
00:27:28,746 --> 00:27:32,839
I believe your hand will get better enough
for you to paint.

272
00:27:32,839 --> 00:27:34,282
Is that true?

273
00:27:34,282 --> 00:27:35,915
Is it, doctor?

274
00:27:37,049 --> 00:27:39,653
Thank you.

275
00:28:12,734 --> 00:28:14,040
Eun Seo.

276
00:28:14,040 --> 00:28:15,162
Jun Seo.

277
00:28:19,968 --> 00:28:23,191
I'm sorry I came here.

278
00:28:25,445 --> 00:28:26,880
Yu Mi is not here.

279
00:28:27,661 --> 00:28:31,015
She went to Seoul.

280
00:28:32,028 --> 00:28:34,208
It's okay even if she's here.
This is my home.

281
00:28:36,388 --> 00:28:37,816
You are good at lying.

282
00:28:45,147 --> 00:28:46,147
Come on in.

283
00:28:53,586 --> 00:28:55,078
Just a second. I'll clean it up.

284
00:29:28,465 --> 00:29:32,916
Do you have two months
before you leave for the U.S?

285
00:29:38,632 --> 00:29:40,220
Did you know that?

286
00:29:42,073 --> 00:29:43,073
Yes.

287
00:29:46,314 --> 00:29:47,315
Jun Seo.

288
00:29:49,921 --> 00:29:51,489
During the two months,

289
00:29:53,511 --> 00:29:56,913
can we meet like this sometimes?

290
00:30:02,870 --> 00:30:09,026
I won't ever get to see you
once you leave.

291
00:30:11,272 --> 00:30:15,385
Can we meet without telling anyone,
for just a few times?

292
00:30:22,838 --> 00:30:24,034
We cannot, can we?

293
00:30:29,510 --> 00:30:30,697
We can't.

294
00:30:31,976 --> 00:30:33,368
We can't do that.

295
00:30:34,230 --> 00:30:35,626
We shouldn't.

296
00:30:40,302 --> 00:30:44,725
Did you come to say that?

297
00:30:47,133 --> 00:30:48,133
No.

298
00:30:49,832 --> 00:30:52,969
Actually, I had a fight
with my brother again.

299
00:30:54,999 --> 00:30:58,129
I think it became a habit
to come here when I had a fight.

300
00:30:58,129 --> 00:30:59,649
Eun Seo.

301
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:02,579
It's fine. I didn't get beaten.

302
00:31:08,413 --> 00:31:09,713
I can't cut it.

303
00:31:21,493 --> 00:31:22,552
It's done.

304
00:31:42,443 --> 00:31:45,203
Aren't you cold, Eun Seo?
Wait for a second.

305
00:31:45,203 --> 00:31:46,517
No, Jun Seo.

306
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:06,555
Take this.

307
00:32:12,288 --> 00:32:14,492
We can't see each other again
before you leave.

308
00:32:15,641 --> 00:32:16,804
Right?

309
00:32:20,681 --> 00:32:21,730
I'll be back.

310
00:32:25,896 --> 00:32:27,051
Don't come back.

311
00:32:31,632 --> 00:32:33,700
I know you're not going to come back.

312
00:32:35,793 --> 00:32:39,802
Don't come back,
and don't reach out to me.

313
00:32:41,090 --> 00:32:46,136
You should just assume,
"She's doing well here."

314
00:32:46,136 --> 00:32:49,250
Just assume that.

315
00:32:50,975 --> 00:32:52,010
Eun Seo.

316
00:32:52,946 --> 00:32:58,751
You should think, "She's doing well here."

317
00:32:58,751 --> 00:33:02,299
Think of me like that.

318
00:33:05,760 --> 00:33:07,307
Please just think of me like that.

319
00:33:10,153 --> 00:33:12,762
Can't you do that?

320
00:33:15,647 --> 00:33:16,969
I will.

321
00:33:19,928 --> 00:33:21,593
I'll think of you, Eun Seo.

322
00:34:06,204 --> 00:34:07,204
Jun Seo.

323
00:34:09,657 --> 00:34:11,075
During the two months,

324
00:34:13,306 --> 00:34:16,925
can we meet like this sometimes?

325
00:34:33,553 --> 00:34:35,541
It got colder.

326
00:34:37,624 --> 00:34:39,372
Yu Mi.

327
00:34:49,985 --> 00:34:51,011
What are you doing?

328
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:55,754
Jun Seo, you need to wear warm clothes.

329
00:34:55,754 --> 00:34:57,140
It got cold.

330
00:35:00,265 --> 00:35:02,011
You don't have a proper jacket.

331
00:35:05,992 --> 00:35:08,419
Where is the jacket?

332
00:35:10,232 --> 00:35:11,682
Which one?

333
00:35:11,682 --> 00:35:15,516
You know my favorite.
The black one with a hoodie.

334
00:35:18,692 --> 00:35:20,902
That one.

335
00:35:22,547 --> 00:35:24,013
Did you take it to a dry cleaner's?

336
00:35:24,604 --> 00:35:28,042
No.

337
00:35:32,839 --> 00:35:34,018
I gave it to Eun Seo.

338
00:35:38,552 --> 00:35:40,137
She came by earlier.

339
00:35:43,199 --> 00:35:45,114
She had only thin clothes.

340
00:35:48,527 --> 00:35:49,994
I see.

341
00:35:54,839 --> 00:35:57,562
You can't even lie.

342
00:35:57,562 --> 00:35:58,951
I hate you for that.

343
00:36:00,419 --> 00:36:02,766
You could've lied for something like that.

344
00:36:07,283 --> 00:36:09,661
I would lie if I were you.

345
00:36:12,869 --> 00:36:13,976
By the way,

346
00:36:15,750 --> 00:36:18,992
I went to the doctor.

347
00:36:25,894 --> 00:36:29,544
He said my hand wouldn't recover.

348
00:36:32,894 --> 00:36:34,009
What should I do?

349
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:53,627
I'm sorry.

350
00:36:55,782 --> 00:36:57,577
I am so sorry, Yu Mi.

351
00:36:59,567 --> 00:37:00,792
It is all right.

352
00:37:02,454 --> 00:37:04,431
It doesn't matter if I can't paint.

353
00:37:06,141 --> 00:37:08,514
Instead, you'll be my hand.

354
00:37:10,806 --> 00:37:12,000
It's okay.

355
00:37:13,268 --> 00:37:14,406
Everything is fine.

356
00:37:19,437 --> 00:37:20,479
I'm sorry.

357
00:37:31,947 --> 00:37:32,974
Hello.

358
00:37:44,514 --> 00:37:45,936
I can't give you this.

359
00:37:46,933 --> 00:37:47,937
Why not?

360
00:37:47,937 --> 00:37:49,663
Because it is an anticancer drug.

361
00:37:49,663 --> 00:37:52,392
I can't give it to you
without a doctor's prescription.

362
00:37:53,182 --> 00:37:55,019
Is it an anticancer drug?

363
00:37:58,208 --> 00:37:59,852
An anticancer drug would be...

364
00:38:02,571 --> 00:38:04,534
used for treating cancer, right?

365
00:38:13,459 --> 00:38:15,587
You need to wait for your turn.
You cannot come in like this.

366
00:38:15,587 --> 00:38:16,875
What is going on?

367
00:38:16,875 --> 00:38:19,338
- Leave, please.
- Who are you?

368
00:38:19,338 --> 00:38:20,992
Does she have cancer?

369
00:38:20,992 --> 00:38:22,451
Does Eun Seo have cancer?

370
00:38:52,691 --> 00:38:53,934
Where is it?

371
00:39:43,186 --> 00:39:45,178
It's all right.

372
00:39:45,178 --> 00:39:48,460
I was going to quit, anyway.

373
00:39:52,537 --> 00:39:53,708
It's fine.

374
00:39:58,034 --> 00:40:02,756
You came to apologize to me, didn't you?

375
00:40:07,521 --> 00:40:09,348
There is no need to apologize.

376
00:40:11,201 --> 00:40:13,076
Compared to what I have done to you...

377
00:40:14,577 --> 00:40:16,973
I will get punished, won't I?

378
00:40:31,201 --> 00:40:32,386
Give me a chance.

379
00:40:38,849 --> 00:40:40,549
Give me one more chance.

380
00:40:42,274 --> 00:40:43,324
Tae Seok?

381
00:40:46,145 --> 00:40:47,277
Give me a chance.

382
00:40:49,008 --> 00:40:52,041
Tell me three reasons you love me.

383
00:40:52,041 --> 00:40:53,227
Then, I will give you a chance.

384
00:41:08,186 --> 00:41:12,299
I don't have any. I can't think of any.

385
00:41:16,979 --> 00:41:19,720
That's why you can't get a chance.

386
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:21,492
You will never get one.

387
00:41:24,337 --> 00:41:27,073
That's too bad.

388
00:41:27,073 --> 00:41:29,596
If you had even one reason,
I would have considered it.

389
00:41:30,274 --> 00:41:31,820
You will never get another chance.

390
00:41:40,209 --> 00:41:45,046
I won't ask you to marry me.

391
00:41:45,046 --> 00:41:50,097
I won't bother or bully you.

392
00:41:52,103 --> 00:41:53,964
I won't ask you to love me.

393
00:41:57,249 --> 00:41:58,363
Your disease,

394
00:42:00,552 --> 00:42:01,971
let me help you beat cancer.

395
00:42:06,585 --> 00:42:08,147
I will fix your disease.

396
00:42:10,256 --> 00:42:11,578
When you beat cancer,

397
00:42:15,337 --> 00:42:16,534
when you get well,

398
00:42:18,684 --> 00:42:19,712
I...

399
00:42:22,493 --> 00:42:23,493
will leave you.

400
00:42:26,943 --> 00:42:29,009
I won't stick around stubbornly,

401
00:42:33,141 --> 00:42:34,512
I'll leave you.

402
00:42:37,398 --> 00:42:39,111
So, please let me get it cured.

403
00:42:46,726 --> 00:42:50,361
How did you know?

404
00:42:52,863 --> 00:42:53,954
How?

405
00:43:20,470 --> 00:43:25,552
You can't die.

406
00:43:27,631 --> 00:43:29,665
I won't forgive you if you die.

407
00:43:33,285 --> 00:43:34,285
Promise me.

408
00:43:37,272 --> 00:43:39,100
When you get well, tell me.

409
00:43:42,785 --> 00:43:44,139
"Tae Seok,"

410
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:49,004
"I don't love you."

411
00:43:52,441 --> 00:43:54,283
"So, please leave me alone."

412
00:43:58,913 --> 00:43:59,923
Promise me.

413
00:44:12,168 --> 00:44:13,993
So, please give me a chance.

414
00:44:17,744 --> 00:44:18,796
No.

415
00:44:19,985 --> 00:44:21,235
I can't.

416
00:44:23,329 --> 00:44:25,787
How can I ask you to do that
after all this?

417
00:44:26,768 --> 00:44:27,940
I can't.

418
00:44:38,429 --> 00:44:39,895
Is this the cancer clinic?

419
00:44:40,451 --> 00:44:43,654
Yes, do you have any rooms available?

420
00:44:44,309 --> 00:44:45,749
Is this Na Rae Nursing Home?

421
00:44:47,028 --> 00:44:50,095
Yes, what's the location?

422
00:45:22,619 --> 00:45:23,619
Mom.

423
00:45:27,309 --> 00:45:32,414
Was Dad in pain?

424
00:45:33,812 --> 00:45:36,365
Did he suffer immensely?

425
00:45:37,435 --> 00:45:40,645
What's wrong with you?
Why are you keep asking about him?

426
00:45:41,507 --> 00:45:42,694
It's nothing.

427
00:45:45,474 --> 00:45:48,559
I wish he hadn't been in much pain.

428
00:45:50,004 --> 00:45:52,787
How could that be possible?

429
00:45:52,787 --> 00:45:55,151
He said it was better to be dead
than to have that pain.

430
00:45:58,867 --> 00:46:01,107
He was also such a crybaby,

431
00:46:01,107 --> 00:46:03,335
so it was an ordeal.

432
00:46:05,484 --> 00:46:06,686
I see.

433
00:46:08,621 --> 00:46:12,303
How long was it before he was in pain
after the diagnosis?

434
00:46:13,115 --> 00:46:16,270
I don't know. I don't remember.

435
00:46:18,410 --> 00:46:21,970
Eun Seo, are you sick?

436
00:46:21,970 --> 00:46:22,973
What?

437
00:46:22,973 --> 00:46:26,438
Why are you sweating so much?

438
00:46:26,438 --> 00:46:27,640
What's wrong?

439
00:47:23,192 --> 00:47:24,386
It's been a long time.

440
00:47:25,343 --> 00:47:28,578
Yes, it has.

441
00:47:30,952 --> 00:47:31,952
How is Yu Mi?

442
00:47:32,984 --> 00:47:35,738
She's doing well.

443
00:47:37,151 --> 00:47:38,386
She went to Seoul.

444
00:47:40,783 --> 00:47:42,122
Isn't it strange?

445
00:47:44,744 --> 00:47:46,747
I thought I would never find you.

446
00:47:49,153 --> 00:47:51,737
But I missed you the most
when in dire times.

447
00:47:55,657 --> 00:47:56,889
Dire times?

448
00:47:59,112 --> 00:48:00,410
Did something happen to you?

449
00:48:04,328 --> 00:48:06,442
Actually, I haven't decided...

450
00:48:08,145 --> 00:48:09,969
whether to tell you or not.

451
00:48:12,311 --> 00:48:13,970
What is it?

452
00:48:19,535 --> 00:48:23,913
Is this about Eun Seo?

453
00:48:28,314 --> 00:48:29,363
No.

454
00:48:34,207 --> 00:48:35,674
I heard you're going to the U.S.

455
00:48:39,543 --> 00:48:40,543
Yes.

456
00:48:42,955 --> 00:48:45,178
Once you get to the U.S.,
don't look back at what happened here.

457
00:48:47,904 --> 00:48:49,003
Don't look back.

458
00:48:50,286 --> 00:48:51,546
Tae Seok.

459
00:48:55,880 --> 00:48:57,073
Eun Seo,

460
00:49:03,191 --> 00:49:04,450
please look after her.

461
00:49:14,392 --> 00:49:15,585
Jun Seo.

462
00:50:08,264 --> 00:50:09,466
Drink this.

463
00:50:24,967 --> 00:50:25,967
Eun Seo.

464
00:50:27,800 --> 00:50:29,061
Jun Seo.

465
00:50:32,435 --> 00:50:36,599
Do you really need to go to the U.S.?

466
00:50:45,850 --> 00:50:51,396
Can you live with me...

467
00:50:53,890 --> 00:50:55,676
just for six months?
